Package: relate
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: embedded agent-native graph database (Cypher 25)
 Relate is an embedded, local graph database written in Rust that
 supports Cypher 25, with an in-memory or transactional filesystem store.
 .
 The relate command provides a REPL, query/load/pull/push tools and
 can serve a database over Bolt, HTTP and MCP.

Package: mcp-server-relate
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, relate (>= ${source:Version})
Description: Relate graph database as an MCP server (stdio)
 Launcher exposing a Relate database to AI assistants over the Model
 Context Protocol on stdio (relate serve --mcp stdio).
 .
 Environment: MCP_SERVER_RELATE_DATABASE (database directory) and
 MCP_SERVER_RELATE_READ_ONLY (true to open the store read-only).

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-relate
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.6.0),
 mcp-server-relate (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Relate MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-relate. Installing it registers
 the mcp-server-relate binary as an available MCP server in the local
 mcprack instance; removing it unregisters it again.
